om Latin commercium. Equivalent to commercie (“commerce, trade”) + -eel (“-al”)."},{"parola":"compagnon","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"companion, friend, partner","termine_origine":"compagnon","catena":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"compagnon","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"compāniō","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*ga-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from French compagnon, derived in turn from Old French compaignon, derived from Late Latin compāniō (“comrade”), derived from com- (“with”) and pānis (“bread”), derived in turn from a calque of Proto-Germanic *ga- (“together, with”) and *hlaibaz (“loaf, bread”). See also compagnie and kompa"},{"parola":"connétable","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"constable of France (supreme commander of the French army or another high-ranking appointee)","termine_origine":"connétable","catena":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"connétable","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"comes stabulī","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-lat","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from French connétable, from Late Latin comes stabulī."},{"parola":"corvee","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"household chores, especially at a camp or barracks","termine_origine":"corvée","catena":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"corvée","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"la-lat","nome":"Late Latin","termine":"conrogāta","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la-lat","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from French corvée, from Middle French corvee, from Old French corvee, from Late Latin conrogāta. Doublet of karwei."},{"parola":"coup","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","i